    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, our offensive core is headlined by **Vinnie Pasquantino** (76.21) and **Josh Naylor** (76.00), both of whom benefit significantly from prime matchups against favorable opposing pitchers. **Vinnie Pasquantino** earns his high floor by attacking Bubba Chandler, where a massive 19% boost from the SP skill gap makes him our most reliable anchor. Similarly, **Josh Naylor** capitalizes on the favorable park factors and a high-leverage matchup against Jose Quintana. **Seiya Suzuki** also remains a must-start at 73.90, fueled by an elite 28-PA BvP history and a strong platoon advantage against the lefty Nick Lodolo. **James Wood** rounds out the elite tier; despite the \"Lineup Pending\" tag, his 69.61 score is heavily inflated by a projectable leadoff spot and his standout 0.412 xwOBA, which suggests he is currently our most efficient engine for Runs.\n\nStrategic priority has been placed on high-upside speed threats, leading to the inclusion of **Mickey Moniak** (71.33). His score is propped up by a 14% platoon edge and the fact that he is facing a slow-delivering pitcher, which historically elevates the success rate for stolen base attempts\u2014a critical variable given our focus on the scarcest category. The most difficult bench decision involved **Austin Riley** (57.80); while he posted a solid efficiency score, he was ultimately edged out by **Max Muncy** (57.76) and **Trevor Story** (55.00). **Max Muncy** secured the final MI spot due to a more favorable SP skill matchup, whereas **Austin Riley** suffered from a bottom-of-the-order projection that penalized his overall output. \n\nWe must remain vigilant regarding the \"Lineup Pending\" statuses for **Gabriel Moreno**, **Moises Ballesteros**, **Cole Young**, **Isaac Paredes**, **Griffin Conine**, and **Corbin Carroll**. **Gabriel Moreno** and **Corbin Carroll** are particularly risky, as they are facing the elite arm of Cam Schlittler (2.88 xERA), which heavily dampens their upside. While **Corbin Carroll** remains in the lineup due to his inherent speed profile, his score of 54.82 is entirely dependent on his dynamic platoon splits; if he is shifted down the order once official lineups drop, we may need to pivot. Otherwise, the roster is optimized to maximize plate appearances and speed efficiency, barring any late-breaking weather alerts.",
